(vector (map (:db/id -1)
  (:adr/doc_type "adr")
  (:adr/id "adr-2609112107-reservation-cljk-host-loader-contract")
  (:adr/topic "cljk-host-loader")
  (:adr/title "Opt-in managed canonical cljk host source patch and qualification")
  (:adr/status "accepted")
  (:adr/date "2026-09-11")
  (:adr/body "The origin-aware loader is merged into the existing managed kbb SCI engine at 90fc125965995b8e8205ac723bf6d432afabe0ed (org-babashka-nbb PR #1), superseding this proposal's standalone nbb 1.4.208 patch. Root npm pins the merged engine; bin/kbb --backend sci remains the canonical host entry. NBB_CLJK_ROOTS or explicit :cljk-roots activates manifest-based platform selection, transitive require/reload and rejection of unknown/ambiguous candidates. Source bytes/paths are unchanged. Qualification: loader 7/23, upstream 50/84, original node 33/106, archive 7/39, seven-witness ref race and run startup/health/stop passed. Inga PR #15 and inga-node PR #3 are merged with merged dependency revisions. Deployment preflight found existing witness snapshots lack voted-view, so activation is blocked rather than discarding safety state. See scripts/nbb-cljk/README.md and qualification.json. This is SCI compatibility, not native Kotoba migration; no byte-identical JS build claim. Owner subsequently authorized a new chain. inga-reservation-20260911-v1 is active on judah/benjamin/simeon/joseph ports 19601-19604, with independent on-host keys and data directories. System LaunchDaemons run as the respective ordinary users. Four-way peer mesh, a single durable winner from two competing smoke records, four offline membership-proof checks, tampered/wrong-chain rejection and w4 restart preserving committed records and vote state all passed. Old chains, keys and snapshots are untouched. Automatic Kotobase archive capture and finalized-prefix service wiring remain unconfigured; this activation is the witness chain, not a claim of live archive persistence or payment execution.")
))
